From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 23:21:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Revert "soc: apple: pmp: release the GPU's AGX vote
 at the sleep's commit"

This reverts commit c400e2cb81 (gpu2-16 of the J604 series).

The GPU now follows Aurora's G16 sleep path (6edf2561ab, Bartosz Nitka),
which keeps its AGX vote through a deep sleep, as measured on a J713
over 8 sleeps. Nothing arms a release at the commit any more, so the
PMP's suspend_late refused every such sleep with the vote held. Without
the check and the release the PMP takes the vote through the sleep as
Aurora's does. Only a firmware-driven suspend reaches this code;
suspend-to-idle does not change.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
